<h1>ARMS — Terms of Service</h1>
<p class="muted">Effective date: 1 November 2026</p>
<h2>The software</h2>
<p>ARMS is open-source software (see the repository license) that runs AI
agents on infrastructure you control and routes their tool calls to the
services you connect. Every connector acts on your account only through
actions you approve: reads run freely where you allow them; writes,
sends, deletes, and other mutations require your explicit approval in
ARMS. For the Gmail connector specifically, that means drafts, sends,
label changes, archives, and trashes wait on your yes.</p>
<h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
<p>Keep your OAuth credentials, vault keys, and database passwords
secret. Use only service accounts you own. The Gmail connector with
restricted Gmail scopes shows Google's "unverified app" screen unless
the app completes Google's verification; by continuing you accept that
this is self-hosted software you operate yourself.</p>
<h2>No warranty</h2>
<p>ARMS is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Service actions
you approve (sends, trashes, label changes, writes to other connectors)
are your actions; review approvals carefully. To the maximum extent
permitted by law, the authors are not liable for any loss arising from
use of the software.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>Material changes to these terms will be posted with a new effective date.
Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>
